cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZenOS-AI or build on its architecture, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ZenOS-AI"
abstract: >-
  ZenOS-AI is a cognitive architecture for a language-model agent that lives
  in a home, built entirely inside Home Assistant. It treats the house as a
  labeled hypergraph, gives the agent an explicit ontology (labels, tool
  contracts, and component declarations) to read it, keeps a digital twin of
  the house current through a background summarization pipeline, renders a
  bounded view of that twin for the agent on each turn, and enforces authority
  outside the model through certification, scope, and live human
  acknowledgement. Its design, and the thesis that an agent's operational
  identity emerges from the graph connections it can realize, are described in
  The Book of Friday, Volume 2, in zenos_ai/docs/architecture.
type: software
